Since nobody else has replied, here is what I know.  (I'm sure there are more
out there who can add to this)

As far as I understand it, there are two facets to this feature.

The halting/strident/strayed (etc., I don't know all of the statuses, does
anyone else?) : This depends on how you act.  Ie, attacking friendly
creatures, killing your pet.

The other depends on how often you pray.  The rule I use that seems to work
is to just not pray until you really need it.

Further spoilers...

It is also possible to "convert" yourself or an altar.  To convert an altar,
make sure you are in good standing with your God, and start sacrificing
monsters ona foreign altar.  This can cause your luck to decrease if you are
sacrificing weak monsters, so try to do it with something somewhat tough,
and of course fresh.  The altar will be yours when you see the message
"the newly consecrated altar glows <color.>"  If you fail, you will see
the message "Unluckily, you sense the power of <your god> decrease" or 
something to that effect.

To convert yourself, do the same thing but while you are in "bad" standing
with your God, ie, someone recently suggested kicking your pet to death
and then sacrificing it's corpse (on the foreign altar).

In short, the best advice I can give is you sacrifice whenever and as much
as possible and don't pray unless you really need to.  I keep seeing people
who insist on praying every X turns in hopes of pleasing their God, but I
suspect that this has an opposite effect.  In my experience, Gods like to
be left alone.

 
